# The payserver-client image this payserver TESTS AGAINST.
#
# Not the one it deploys: the frontend deploys on its own cadence,
# from payserver-client via central-infrastructure. This pin exists so E2E runs
# against a known frontend rather than a moving target.
#
# The frontend lives in its own repository (gcannelloni/payserver-client) and
# publishes its own image, so it no longer shares this repo's commit sha. This
# file is the pin that replaces that coupling: an exact, immutable tag, moved
# deliberately, reviewed like any other change.
#
# Do NOT point this at `latest`. The whole reason the per-commit tag exists is
# that a moving tag makes "which frontend is live" unanswerable and a rollback
# a rebuild. The same argument that gave the server images an immutable tag
# applies here, more so now that the frontend can change without this repo
# moving at all.
#
# To move it: pick a tag from
#   https://github.com/gcannelloni/payserver-client/pkgs/container/payserver-client
# and open a PR. CI pulls exactly this image for the E2E run, so a frontend that
# breaks the payment flow fails here rather than on testnet.
#
# Because deploys are separate, this can drift from what is live. That is the
# tradeoff of independent cadence, and it is deliberate - but if it drifts far,
# E2E stops telling you anything about production.
#
# The gap is meant to be bumped deliberately, not held at zero. The pin exists
# so E2E has a fixed target; a pin that tracks main on every client commit is
# a moving target again, and that is exactly what it replaces. Expect some
# distance, and bump when it is worth the selector work: move the pin and the
# e2e selectors in the same commit, since a client rename leaves one half
# looking for controls the other no longer labels that way. The drift job in
# ci.yml stays non-blocking on purpose, and its warning is not the report: the
# deploy host's scheduled-check watcher measures the same distance and sends it,
# with the count, to the message bus each time it crosses a step (10, 25, 50,
# 100 commits), so a large gap does not look like a small one.
ghcr.io/randomcash/payserver-client:sha-ca147e2
